  "_label": "pack",
  "referred_to_by": [
    {
      "type": "LinguisticObject",
      "classified_as": [
        {
          "id": "aat:300435416",
          "type": "Type",
          "_label": "descriptive note"
        }
      ],
      "content": "pack: a packing unit and measure for dry goods, flax, cloth, yarn, candlewick and similar wares — both a physical unit of transport of no particular size and, for some commodities, a measure of definite size (flax: 150 bales = 20 cwt at 112 lb./cwt; candlewick: 20 cwt; Irish yarn: 4 cwt at 120 lb./cwt; Cologne thread: 30 dozen lb.) (Zupko 270-1). See also packet, fardel, truss; for pack-thread see packthrede; for the pack-needle and packduck see those."
    }
  ],
